{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 45,
  "title": "Books and reading",
  "description": "Name the parts of a book, and say what you read.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Books are made of parts, and each part has a name. This unit gives you the nouns and the verbs that go with them.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El periódico, el título, el autor and el cuento are masculine. La lectura, la revista, la página, la letra, la frase y la idea are feminine. La lectura is the reading, and it is also the activity: la lectura es buena.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el periódico",
            "en": "the newspaper"
          },
          {
            "es": "la página",
            "en": "the page"
          },
          {
            "es": "el autor",
            "en": "the author"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What is in the book",
        "body": "Estar says where a thing is, and the parts of a book are things: el título está en la portada, la frase está en la página. Leer is to read, and it is a regular -ar verb: leo, lees, lee.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "leo el periódico por la mañana",
            "en": "I read the newspaper in the morning"
          },
          {
            "es": "la página está en el libro",
            "en": "the page is in the book"
          },
          {
            "es": "el cuento es de un autor español",
            "en": "the story is by a Spanish author"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
